 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Mathlib has `abbrev IsBipartite (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop := G.Colorable 2` (Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Bipartite.lean:288). The nearby simple-graph corollaries in TauCeti/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Matching/Regular.lean:84,137 take `(hbip : G.IsBipartite)`. `SimpleGraph.isBipartition_ofSimpleGraph_iff` (TauCeti/Combinatorics/Graph/Bipartition.lean:350) already converts between the two forms. Roadmap 6.9 (README.md:812-815) asks only for simple-graph corollaries and does not require a displayed bipartition on the simple-graph side.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Matching/EdgeColoring.lean",
   "fix": "State it as `theorem lineGraph_colorable_iff_maxDegree_le [Fintype V] [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hG : G.IsBipartite) : G.lineGraph.Colorable k \u2194 G.maxDegree \u2264 k`. In the proof, turn the 2-colouring into a covering pair with `IsBipartite.exists_isBipartiteWith` (or the colour classes, whose union is `univ`), convert it with `SimpleGraph.isBipartition_ofSimpleGraph_iff`, then apply the multigraph theorem.",
   "issue": "`lineGraph_colorable_iff_maxDegree_le` is labelled a simple-graph corollary, but it asks for `{L R : Finset \u21a5(Graph.ofSimpleGraph G).vertexSet} (hLR : (Graph.ofSimpleGraph G).IsBipartition L R)`. That is the multigraph hypothesis passed through unchanged. Callers need a covering bipartition written as finsets of a subtype, which is stronger to supply than Mathlib's `G.IsBipartite`.",
   "line": 75
  }
 ],
